From: Radeon24 <Radeon24@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: fsoc1: add Fortinet FortiSOC1 platform

The FortiSOC1 is the SoC of the Fortinet FortiGate 60C appliance. It is a
Faraday FA626TE core with stock Faraday peripherals (FTINTC010, FTTMR010,
FTUART010, FTWDT010), all supported by existing drivers. Its network
processor is the only custom block.

Like ARCH_MOXART, the platform needs no mach- directory: the generic DT
machine descriptor is enough, so this only adds the Kconfig symbol.

The stock boot loader passes ATAGs and cannot load a device tree, so a
bootable kernel needs ARM_APPENDED_DTB and ARM_ATAG_DTB_COMPAT. These are
user-visible boot options: they are left to the kernel configuration and
not selected here. The help text says so.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Radeon24 <Radeon24@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 arch/arm/Kconfig.platforms | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

--- a/arch/arm/Kconfig.platforms
+++ b/arch/arm/Kconfig.platforms
@@ -87,6 +87,23 @@ config MACH_ASM9260
 	help
 	  Support for Alphascale ASM9260 based platform.
 
+config ARCH_FSOC1
+	bool "Fortinet FortiSOC1"
+	depends on ARCH_MULTI_V4
+	depends on CPU_LITTLE_ENDIAN
+	select CPU_FA526
+	select FARADAY_FTINTC010
+	select FTTMR010_TIMER
+	help
+	  Support for the Fortinet FortiSOC1, found in the FortiGate 60C
+	  appliance. It is built around a Faraday FA626TE core and stock
+	  Faraday peripherals: FTINTC010 interrupt controller, FTTMR010
+	  timer, FTUART010 serial port and FTWDT010 watchdog.
+
+	  The stock boot loader cannot pass a device tree. It only passes
+	  ATAGs, so a kernel for this platform needs ARM_APPENDED_DTB and
+	  ARM_ATAG_DTB_COMPAT.
+
 menuconfig ARCH_HPE
 	bool "HPE SoC support"
 	depends on ARCH_MULTI_V7
